     "updated": "2021-02-16T16:10:58.131-0400"
    },
    {
     "author": {
      "accountId": "6089a55c52a3d400690692f7",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/6089a55c52a3d400690692f7/7a62c587-b0f1-4cd4-982c-21b3837dc64a/16",
       "24x24": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/6089a55c52a3d400690692f7/7a62c587-b0f1-4cd4-982c-21b3837dc64a/24",
       "32x32": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/6089a55c52a3d400690692f7/7a62c587-b0f1-4cd4-982c-21b3837dc64a/32",
       "48x48": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/6089a55c52a3d400690692f7/7a62c587-b0f1-4cd4-982c-21b3837dc64a/48"
      },
      "displayName": "Ralf Claussnitzer",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=6089a55c52a3d400690692f7",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": {
      "content": [
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "I was not so much thinking about RDF in particular but that could be a one side of the same problem. What I was actually thinking about is invalid XML documents (my use case mostly). Or more general: ",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "marks": [
           {
            "type": "em"
           }
          ],
          "text": "POSTed content that does violate the specified request content type",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "text": ". For example sending a GIF with content type application/jpeg. Currently there is no way to protect Fedora from this. ",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "In the end I will need to implement an extra-Fedora HTTP endpoint to check the transmitted files against very specific content types rules. For example, we use a custom content type application/vnd.qucosa.mets+xml which defines certain structural constraints.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "Since this is very application specific it should not be included in Fedora, I agree. I'm actually not sure  if API-X is the appropriate solution for this. There is Camel now and it can produce HTTP endpoints for integrating with Fedora.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       }
      ],
      "type": "doc",
      "version": 1
     },
